      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "State animal: Wild Buffalo | State bird: Pahadi Myna | State tree: Sal | State flower: Gaur Orchid",
        "Highest peak: Gaurlata (1,225 m), Surguja",
        "Longest river in CG: Mahanadi (from Sihawa, Gariaband)",
        "Widest waterfall: Chitrakoot Falls (on Indravati, Bastar)",
        "Only tin ore producing state: Chhattisgarh",
        "Bhilai Steel Plant: SAIL; Soviet collaboration; produces 60% of India's rails",
        "Forest cover: ~44% of state area (one of highest in India)",
        "Tribal population: ~30.6% (42 scheduled tribes, 5 PVTGs)",
        "Bastar Dussehra: World's longest Dussehra (75 days); not based on Ramayan",
        "Ghotul system: Muria tribe's youth dormitory social institution"
